#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-inverted-flight.rst:5
#: fb7c7d6540f84b3da724613c182ea0ed
msgid "Inverted Flight"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-inverted-flight.rst:7
#: d83b9b5f880f49f398e589e72374aef0
msgid ""
"Since helicopters, including dual rotor and heli-quads, are capable of "
"generating negative thrust (negative collective) they have the capability"
" of flying, even hovering, inverted. This, of course, requires that the "
"vehicle is capable of generating sufficient thrust while inverted and is "
"setup to do so (see :ref:`traditional-helicopter-aerobatic-setup`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-inverted-flight.rst:9
#: 96e69a39df234f8cb2de14921abe12e4
msgid "Inverted flight can be commanded in two different ways:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-inverted-flight.rst:11
#: 7a2f046e0887497ea581d240dc40a52c
msgid ""
"Under pilot attitude control in ACRO mode which requires the pilot to "
"push the collective stick down to climb while inverted and the pitch "
"control is oriented to the inverted aircraft as well, or"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-inverted-flight.rst:12
#: 671da4e7d87843ba87dc8ecfca56e876
msgid ""
"Under ArduPilot attitude stabilization control, in STABILIZE, ALTHOLD, "
"LOITER, and AUTO modes using the ``RCx_OPTION`` invert switch function "
"\"43\". This merely flips the effective orientation of the IMU to be "
"inverted and the vehicle follows. It will stabilise the vehicle with a "
"roll of 180 degrees from normal whenever inverted flight is enabled. "
"While inverted, collective is used normally in STABILIZE, ALTHOLD and "
"LOITER where pushing up on the collective causes the inverted helicopter "
"to climb away from the ground.  Pitch control is also used as though the "
"aircraft is upright."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-inverted-flight.rst:15
#: 4def4dcae21d407592948653b4b860f4
msgid "Notes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-inverted-flight.rst:17
#: fa6ef0d34ea0437d883d5f74019c66f4
msgid ""
"GPS required modes such as LOITER and AUTO require good GPS performance "
"which may be impacted adversely if the GPS is facing down for long "
"periods, especially hover precision. Dual blended GPSes oriented such "
"that one has a \"sky-view\" while inverted can ameliorate this. In "
"extreme cases, EKF failsafes might occur with undesirable effects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-inverted-flight.rst:18
#: 961ec3b2c7ed4c3799025f38f72d98ac
msgid ""
"Negative collective range is not impacted using the invert switch, ie it "
"becomes the effective climb control so be sure there is sufficient range."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-inverted-flight.rst:21
#: be25cf1e3e04467d8417cffd0eb0bc35
msgid "Setup of the inverted flight feature"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-inverted-flight.rst:23
#: c997eb6a0b5a44628cabcc3658c7a372
msgid ""
"The inverted flight feature is initiated by setting an RC channel via "
"RCx_OPTION parameter.  The RCx_OPTION parameter allows you to configure a"
" transmitter switch to enable inverted flight for helicopters. To enable "
"it, choose a RC input channel which is not being used for anything else, "
"and setup your transmitter to give a PWM value larger than 1750 when a "
"previously unused 2 position switch is enabled, and a value below 1200 "
"when it is not enabled.  For example, if channel 7 is currently unused, "
"and you set :ref:`RC7_OPTION<RC7_OPTION>` to InvertedFlight (which has "
"value 43) then if your transmitter sends 1900 on channel 7 the helicopter"
" will flip upside down and continue flying in whatever mode it is in, but"
" with the helicopter inverted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-inverted-flight.rst:25
#: a4a6f8b82dc3484c8664456134f2b7a4
msgid ""
"Be sure to setup pitch and roll rate limits.  This will keep the attitude"
" controller from commanding unachievable roll or pitch rates.  It is "
"recommended in STABILIZE or ACRO that you command max roll and pitch "
"rates.  Pull the flight logs and determine what is the maximum pitch and "
"roll rate the aircraft can achieve.  Then set "
":ref:`ATC_RATE_R_MAX<ATC_RATE_R_MAX>` for max roll rate and "
":ref:`ATC_RATE_P_MAX<ATC_RATE_P_MAX>` for max pitch rate.  If you are "
"unable to determine the max rates then be conservative and set them to "
"120 deg/s initially."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-inverted-flight.rst:28
#: 748395ee3958444d8c89451adddb0ffa
msgid "Tips"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-inverted-flight.rst:30
#: 6556a15c728240c5a713e7b4eae7e34d
msgid "Here are some general tips about inverted flight"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-inverted-flight.rst:32
#: 45f70e6ad8a5417082435830d0fdb5ca
msgid ""
"Try it out in simulation first to get used to it, and ensure your "
"transmitter is setup right."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-inverted-flight.rst:34
#: a2f7b46ab8534d88ac4d55c20f5e841f
msgid ""
"make sure you have plenty of height before engaging or disengaging "
"inverted flight for the first time. The aircraft should not lose much "
"altitude during the transition but it is worth having the extra altitude "
"incase something unexpected happens.  As you get more comfortable in the "
"aircraft's ability to transition from upright to inverted and vice-versa,"
" then you can lower the altitude where the transition is made."
msgstr ""

